-- IELTS 5.0 (B1): the bridge from Foundation to 6.0. New Reading, Listening and Writing points, and lessons for the B1
-- grammar and vocabulary points that moved here. Every point gets a lesson and a practice set of three or more objective
-- questions; every chặng gets a final test; the course gets a course test. Listening follows the transcripts of reused
-- recordings.

-- New points and their prerequisites.

-- Reading: skimming paragraphs.

A. Ten years ago, Elmford had no public gardens at all. Today there are six, and more than three hundred residents grow their own vegetables on small plots rented from the town council for twenty pounds a year.

B. The gardens are popular with retired people, but young families have joined too. Parents say their children now know where food comes from, and many schools bring classes to the gardens in spring.

C. There are problems, however. The waiting list for a plot is now two years long, and some gardeners complain that water from the taps is not enough in dry summers. The council plans to put in rain tanks next year.', 'VALID');
