A. Many people change their phone every two years, even when the old one still works. Most of these phones end up in a drawer at home.

B. A small company in Leeds now collects unwanted phones, repairs them and sells them again at half the price of a new model. Each phone is tested for a whole day before it goes on sale.

C. The company says that buying a repaired phone saves energy and reduces waste. It also gives one phone to a local charity for every ten it sells.', 'VALID');
