-- Reading: short-answer questions.

The ferry to Holm Island leaves the harbour four times a day in summer and twice a day in winter. The crossing takes forty minutes. Passengers can take bicycles on board free of charge, but cars must be booked at least one day before travelling. There is a small cafe on the upper deck that sells hot drinks and sandwiches. On windy days the ferry may be cancelled, so travellers are advised to check the harbour website before they leave home.', 'VALID');
