-- Course test: Reading and Listening.

A. For twenty years there was no night train between the capital and the northern coast. Passengers had to fly or drive for nine hours.

B. Last month the service began again. The train leaves at ten in the evening and arrives at seven the next morning. Each cabin has two beds and a small washbasin.

C. Tickets sold quickly, especially at weekends. The railway company now plans to add more carriages in summer, when demand is highest.', 'VALID');
